    "turn_idx": 1,
    "turn_text": "Welcome to Security Dilemma. I'm John Allen Gay joined here by my co-host and producer, Patrick Carver Fox. Today we speak with a member of Congress who's been a champion on issues like reforming the outdated authorizations for use of military force. that have seen congressional power usurped by president after president taking away the power that Congress has under the Constitution to decide when and where America goes to war. He's been a champion on reforming that, a champion on reforming surveillance powers. And he's been a thought leader within Congress in talking about what a new direction in U.S. foreign policy might look like, how in particular on the right, there needs to be a turn away from the neoconservative moment of the post-9-11 Iraq War. era. Congressman Warren Davidson represents Ohio's 8th District. He serves on the House Foreign Affairs Committee, among others, and he is an alumnus of the United States Military Academy and a former Army Ranger. So join us on security dilemma as we speak with Congressman Warren Davidson. Representative Davidson, last night you were one of 14 Republicans to vote against a $17.6 billion aid package that Speaker Johnson had proposed for Israel. What was your thinking on that vote?",
