  {
    "episode_id": 84578,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/4/84578.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 5,
    "turn_text": "Yeah, so look, there's one body in America that's supposed to declare war, and that's Congress. The Constitution is clear on that. The Founding Fathers were clear on that. Federalist 69 is maybe the most clear on that. So Congress needs to expect that we make these decisions. Ultimately, and why? Because it's important that you don't have just a small portion of the country or just the military, particularly an all volunteer military, be the only force that's actually in combat. If we go to war, it really does involve the whole country. It risks the whole country. And we should actually commit to go to the war as a country so that the nation as a war not just a handful of people. And I think when we do that, then we're more reluctant to do it, and we're certainly more reluctant to do it without asking, what exactly are we trying to accomplish? How are we planning to go about doing that? And how do we say we've succeeded or failed? I mean, how do we define the mission? And we're doing none of those kinds of things right now with our involvement. And if you say, oh, well, they should respond, they were attacked by Houthis. Well, some people were attacked by Houthis. And of course you have a right to self-defense. That's not what I'm talking about. If you have time to build an international coalition and plan offensive attacks, you have time to come to Congress. And when it comes to protecting the shipping lanes, I think that an international coalition that agrees that America doesn't fund this whole thing and doesn't pay it. We shouldn't be the nation's police, but we also shouldn't be the We shouldn't be the world's police, and we also shouldn't be the world's coast guard, right? But the idea that the shipping lanes should be navigable and trusted, I think that's something that I would vote for, but I should be voting on it, not just reading about it in the news like everyone else.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_02",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
    "explicit_propositions": [
