        "text": "Congress is the sole body in America authorized to declare war according to the Constitution.",
        "confidence": 0.97
      },
      {
        "text": "Currently, there is insufficient clarity around war objectives, strategy, success criteria, and mission definition.",
        "confidence": 0.96
      },
      {
        "text": "The Founding Fathers intended Congress to have exclusive power over declaring war.",
        "confidence": 0.95
      },
      {
        "text": "Self-defense against Houthi attacks is legitimate and justified under international law.",
