      },
      {
        "text": "It is essential that the entire country be involved in decisions to go to war, not just a small group or the military.",
        "confidence": 0.94
      },
      {
        "text": "National commitment to war requires broad consensus because war affects the entire country.",
        "confidence": 0.93
      },
      {
        "text": "Federalist Paper 69 clearly supports Congressional control over declarations of war.",
        "confidence": 0.92
      },
      {
        "text": "When the nation collectively commits to war, decision-making becomes more cautious and deliberate.",
