  {
    "episode_id": 84578,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/4/84578.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 11,
    "turn_text": "You talked about how we still have these authorizations for use of military force in place from 2001, the post-9-11 AUMF and from 2002, the Iraq War AUMF, and that Congress has been kind of coasting on these rather than freshly debating, even those wars, let alone new questions of war and peace. Why do you think that is? Because the Constitution gives you guys the power to make those decisions. So why don't folks want to make those decisions?",
