  {
    "episode_id": 84578,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/4/84578.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 15,
    "turn_text": "Yeah, I mean, it's been shocking to see how our troops are out there displaying a lot of courage and bravery, and yet members of Congress aren't ready to do the same thing, not even physical courage, physical bravery, in terms of defending and making decisions about what those troops should be doing in the first place. But I wanted to pivot over to Eastern Europe. So the Biden administration on Friday responded to your May 2023 letter demanding that there be a defined strategy for America's support for Ukraine in their war with Russia. The administration stated that our goal is for Ukraine to emerge from this war as a democratic, independent, sovereign, and prosperous nation that can deter and defend itself against future aggression. So is this an attainable goal? And are you satisfied by the response that you got?",
