  {
    "episode_id": 84578,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/4/84578.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 20,
    "turn_text": "Well, certainly I've introduced the Define the Mission Act in the House. Got a lot of good co-sponsors in the House. Senator Mike Lee carried the Senate companion to it. And this is a restatement of the vote that we had on the National Defense Authorization last July. I referenced that earlier in our conversation. We got 129 votes on that. And that was just limiting, limiting a little bit of funding that goes through NATO. and DOD. So in this case, you're talking about the whole ball of wax, but before we give them another dime, there's nothing someone in Ukraine can answer for this. It has to be our own administration. Tell us the mission. And the response to the letters, a big accelerant of that. Frankly, my colleague, Mike Garcia, Naval Academy Navy fighter pilot, he had put a kind of booklet together that, you know, used a negotiation with the administration and build a coalition of some of the defense hawks to kind of push the same narrative and say, well, we're probably not going to get the law passed that Davidson's asking for, but I essentially have the same question. What is the mission? So you go to the point of the 18% who have served in our military, we're used to saying that upfront, like, what is the mission? What do you want me to accomplish? And so I think that hasn't even been answered. That hasn't stopped the Senate apparently from moving forward with plans to fund it. But I do think it's going to stop the House from even remotely considering it. And when we do agree on the mission, or some consensus comes together to do that, it may be included in some part of our funding for our government. But again, I don't think the House is likely to bring it up unless we commit to secure our own borders and we fund our own government. I think there's just not going to be the votes from the majority party anyway to put it to the floor unless we can say we funded America and we're willing to defend America.",
